  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759184,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1000 Miglia (Commodore Amiga)\n\nStep back in time to 1927 and experience the thrill of the inaugural 1000 Miglia, a legendary Italian automobile race! Developed by Simulmondo and published by Kaneko, this Amiga title captures the spirit of the historic rally, challenging players to navigate the picturesque Italian countryside in classic 1930s race cars. \n\nWhile the game leans towards arcade-style gameplay rather than a realistic racing simulation, it was groundbreaking for its time, attempting to model car behavior under varying racing conditions. Don't expect cutting-edge sound quality, but do prepare for a unique and challenging experience. \n\nRelive the history of this demanding race, originally deemed so difficult its creators believed it would be a one-off event.  Compete against the clock and the environment in this unusual racing title, a fascinating glimpse into early racing game development and a tribute to a truly iconic motorsport event."
    },
